-Gold sellers;
-IMC is a company that can't keep up with their word. I.e.: saying that they'll allow server transfers in the future when regional servers are released. Then, they say transfer won't be possible.
-Bugged quests;
-A lot of crashing during cutscenes;
-And much more.
I could stay here forever listing the cons, but they're simply too many. Sorry.

THIS GAME IS HIGHLY ADDICTIVE
if you want to throw away your life, but don't want to use real drugs, play ToS.
Initial warning;
If you expect game will carry you to "end game" with quests and give you some "end game" dungeons/raids, DO NOT play ToS, because you HAVE to grind here, its better if you go play wow or any other wow clone.
Altough game is released, it's still developing for pvp/gvg, new level caps etc.
Pros;
It has amazing art/music, diverse class system to play around,mostly oldschool players(decent community), weird exp curve(exp requirements drops drastically at levels 16,46,86 on so on) for levels which feels kind of rewarding in my opinion.
Developers listen the community, they take suggestion, give compensations if something unexpected happens, and thats a really big (+) for me.
Cons;
Trade restrictions(that's all) but its really annoying.Developers say it's there for the purpose of blocking gold sellers but, it hurts community(paid player or free player) more than it hurts gold sellers.It destroys the purpose of crafting classes(such as alchemists),you ran out of pot in dungeon ? too bad, better use those sweet bacis attacks because noone can share their pot with you. That one (-) alone really takes away some feels of mmo, but I still hope developers will find a way to fix it.

